151980	152190	151977	151977	he	197	" surely this must be God 's judgment upon the purposeless , vacillating life I led up to the seventh day of last September . Surely this awful responsibility has been forced upon me in order that I may humble myself to an offended Providence , and confess that a man can not choose his own life . He can not say , ' I will take existence lightly , and keep out of the way of the wretched , mistaken , energetic creatures , who fight so heartily in the great battle . ' He can not say , ' I will stop in the tents while the strife is fought , and laugh at the fools who are trampled down in the useless struggle . ' He can not do this . He can only do , humbly and fearfully , that which the Maker who created him has appointed for him to do . If he has a battle to fight , let him fight it faithfully ; but woe betide him if he skulks when his name is called in the mighty muster - roll , woe betide him if he hides in the tents when the tocsin summons him to the scene of war ! "
